title: How to read these diagrams
route: Every diagram uses the same sixteen shapes and colours
intro: One example flow that uses every shape once. The shape tells you what kind of step it is; the colour tells you who does it.
dir: LR
---
start s1 "Start\nA sidebar click or a link"
screen sc1 "Screen\nA page the person sees"
click c1 "Person clicks\nA button, row or key"
input i1 "Person enters\nTypes, picks, drops a file"
overlay o1 "Pop-up\nDrawer, modal or menu"
process p1 "System step\nThe app validates or updates"
agent a1 "FLO / agent\nAutomated work (Reader, Scribe...)"
decision d1 "Decision\nEvery exit is labelled"
store st1 "Data saved\nA record is created or changed"
doc dc1 "Document\nLetter, brief, report"
toast t1 "Message\nA toast or banner"
ext x1 "Outside party\nPayer, referrer, EMR"
wait w1 "Wait\nTime passes"
goto g1 "Continues elsewhere\nNames the other diagram"
end e1 "End (done)"
endx e2 "End (stopped)"
s1 --> sc1 --> c1 --> i1 --> o1 --> p1 --> a1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| st1 --> dc1 --> t1 --> x1 --> w1 --> g1
d1 -->|No| e2
g1 --> e1
